Markets, organisations, and economic coordination (@markets-organisations-and-economic-coordination: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_36S6PP6AZYT11CGX09K042DRGY
This material investigates how households, firms, public bodies, and other organisations make and coordinate economic decisions. It connects prices, incentives, competition, market power, contracts, labour, public goods, external effects, and alternative arrangements for cooperation. Compare models with the institutions and observations relevant to a case, introducing equations or optimisation only when used. Link local decisions to social relationships, political rules, distribution, and the production or maintenance systems followed through Ergon.

**Parent:** [Political-Economy](../Political-Economy.lingua#r_2WPG1Y767BM24Z0K4BY6Y6T62W).
